{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Do not say.</b> He further commands and warns the wise man to rejoice in his portion, even if he is poor, as written above, 'What advantage does the poor man have?' And he says: let him not engage in matters of acquiring wealth, but only what suffices him. Nor should he be angry because a fool has more wealth than he; let him be long-spirited and not say, 'What was,' as fools say when they fall from greatness, that the world has turned upside down. For the discerning will know that the days are the same and the supernal configurations are the same — only the recipients change, each man according to his portion."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:05.126733640Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}